  "label": "The Belgian King knew about the murder plots at the time - and did nothing

The Belgian King knew of plans for his assassination and did nothing; the CIA ordered its employees to take care of the disposal of the new Prime Minister, who wanted a completely different Congo, one whose riches were to benefit all [Gruppe 1]. After only three months in office, Lumumba was removed from power. He fled, was captured, and was kidnapped to the secessionist and resource-rich province of Katanga, where he was shot - under the supervision of Belgian officers. A few days later, two Belgian colonial police officers dug Lumumba's body out of the provisional grave, drove it deep into the bush, dismembered it, and dissolved it in acid.

One of the two, Gérard Soete, took two teeth and a finger bone as souvenirs. When he died in 2000, he left behind at least one tooth, which his daughter proudly showed to journalists. For a long time, the Belgian judiciary was little bothered by this; only when the journalist Ludo De Witte legally demanded the surrender of the tooth did they become active. For a long time, the tooth lay in a safe of the highest judicial authority, which would probably have preferred to return it to the family as inconspicuously as possible."
